<section id="r9-failure"><h2>What failed, and where the time went</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><div class="kicker">Authenticated failure</div><h3>A cache hit was rejected by a schedule witness</h3><p>The exact return ended with <code>B051_SCHEDULE_EXACT_FULL_READBACK_REQUIRED</code> during <code>04_latest_source_refresh</code>. The consumer required a fresh network readback where the persistent cache supplied authenticated local bytes.</p><p>The check must verify the original exact content and readback provenance. A cache reuse must not be relabeled as a new S3 request or an earlier quote.</p></article><article class="panel"><div class="kicker">Actual CPU result</div><h3>The ready scientific queue was never reached</h3><p>The launcher requested a twelve-core ceiling on a 48-vCPU host. Peak actual ready demand and reservations stayed at <strong>one CPU</strong>; the measured process-tree peak was <strong>1.000436 cores</strong>.</p><p>No independent scientific worker or native scientific callback started. A configured worker ceiling, locally tested queue or synthetic contract check cannot establish twelve-core utilization.</p></article></div>
