<section id="r9-cache"><h2>Measured reuse, with the counter boundaries exposed</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>118 verified reads reused local data</h3><p>The instrumented store reused <strong>1,396,887,267 bytes</strong> from persistent local content. The lower cache layer reports 119 hits and 1,396,887,736 bytes, including one extra small receipt access. Those counter scopes are not added together.</p><p>The original content identities and readback clocks remain preserved. This is actual cache evidence from R8, although a completed identical-data scientific rerun has not yet passed its separate acceptance gate.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Two full S3 readbacks remain distinct</h3><p>The store made <strong>two verified full GETs totaling 24,079,252 bytes</strong>, taking a reported 0.341 seconds. They checked the newly published executable and a small receipt. Return persistence uses a separate transfer scope.</p><p>The result does not mean that all network activity was zero, nor that cache reads refreshed provider quotes. No paid historical acquisition or new market comparison is credited here.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="r9-logs"><h2>Live observation worked during the failed attempt</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>55 captured events and 26 heartbeats</h3><p>The returned <code>LIVE_EXECUTION.jsonl</code> contains <strong>55 valid event records</strong>. Its 26 heartbeats have a maximum captured event timestamp gap of <strong>10.010604 seconds</strong>; the logger’s internal monotonic cadence clock reports <strong>10.010606 seconds</strong>. The paired human log captured 141,986 bytes, and JSONL captured 248,052 bytes.</p><p>The terminal flush was acknowledged at publisher sequence 1756. Validation reported no errors. Events after capture remain external; this is an authenticated bounded prefix.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Attribution and cost stay qualified</h3><p>The original logger retained an older R7 text label. This page identifies the actual R8 executable through its exact SHA-256, and R9 corrects the bound release label. Original log bytes remain unchanged.</p><p>The returned whole-instance invocation estimate is <strong>$0.1652</strong> at a verified $2.57/hour rate. It is an estimate, not an invoice or an allocation of cost across overlapping workloads.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="r9-repair"><h2>What the prepared R9 continuation repairs</h2><ol><li><strong>Schedule cache provenance.</strong> Accept exact cached bytes only with the verified original readback witness; reject missing, malformed or mismatched evidence.</li><li><strong>Authenticated prior recovery and receipt reuse.</strong> Restore explicit admission of the authenticated prior-recovery import. Reuse parsed receipt proofs while fully hashing every current file at each existing recheck boundary. The legacy adoption chain still runs; a reduction of its observed 181.608 seconds has not been verified.</li><li><strong>Native validation caching.</strong> Support explicit conda or installed egg file inventories when setuptools has no wheel <code>RECORD</code>. Changed files and metadata still invalidate reuse.</li><li><strong>Ready-queue admission and live identity.</strong> Retain safe shared twelve-core admission, verify the startup-to-ready-queue route and report the current release in the bound live logger.</li></ol><p id="r9-receipt-benchmark"><strong>Measured local receipt subset:</strong> a replay of 112 captured JSON receipt/metadata files (666,672 distinct bytes) took a median 0.082406 seconds in the baseline and 0.034488 seconds with parsed-proof reuse, a <strong>2.389× speedup for that subset only</strong>. This measures local byte-reading, strict JSON parsing and recursive receipt proof work. It does not measure the full owner adoption phase, SageMaker storage, S3, model deserialization or scientific training.</p><details id="r9-verification"><summary>Inspect verification scope and source fingerprint</summary><p id="r9-validation">__R9_VALIDATION__</p><p>Prepared executable SHA-256: <code id="r9-source">__R9_SOURCE__</code>.</p><p>Local engineering checks receive zero sports-fit credit. R9 owner execution, simultaneous scientific fits, sustained CPU utilization, full-season coverage and new forecasts remain unverified.</p></details></section>
